# Banter in Memory's Rest (story/banter.gd plays this file only where a place's region is memorys_rest): one exchange between two or three companions about what is in
# front of them in one place, gated on that place (`at:`) and on the story's state so a remark never runs ahead of the chapter. Played now and then on entering
# an area, once each; an exchange nobody present can speak comes out empty and is skipped.
# Drafted by Gemini (docs/plans/gemini_companions/), edited; every edit is listed in the README there. Lines are unvoiced until the voice lane reads them.


~ mr_shore_01_delphine_rook
if name:delphine_ravelle and name:rook_coldwake and at:mr_shore and not flag.lethica_slain
interject name:delphine_ravelle: An hour of sucking mud and not a footlight in sight, Rook. Those briars have chewed my hem.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Shingle drains better than marsh, I'll grant it. Nobody's cleared the reeds round the landing, though.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: And that driftwood carving with the jawbone. Your Foolishness is jealous of the dental work.
interject name:rook_coldwake: An unlicensed effigy, and a rowboat left unchained. Still, beats standing in the bog.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Just row steady toward those violet windows, before the damp gets into my sawdust.
endif
-> END

~ mr_isle_02_silas_tobin
if name:silas_vane and name:tobin_hayward and at:mr_isle and not flag.lethica_slain
interject name:silas_vane: Fancy lettering over the iron doors, Tobin. A house that polite is hiding a rigged shoe.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Look at the shallows instead. Black irises growing fat in cold rot, and a willow choking itself.
interject name:silas_vane: Four rowboats at the pilings and nobody to take our coats. Even that owl looks like he lost his shirt.
interject name:tobin_hayward: The forecourt smells of wet lime and old fever. We're walking into a blighted orchard.
endif
-> END

~ mr_ground_03_lucan_cordelia
if name:lucan_houndstooth and name:cordelia_skein and at:mr_ground and not flag.lethica_slain
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Good heavens, Cordelia, the chamomile is practically aggressive. Barnaby has flattened his ears at those violet tubes.
interject name:cordelia_skein: That hum is badly out of tune, darling. Ruinous for the nerves. But what tidy masks the orderlies wear.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: A gentleman prefers to see the face of the creature he's addressing.
interject name:cordelia_skein: It's a parlour trick to keep the pulse slow. Stay off the floral chairs, Lucan.
endif
-> END

~ mr_upper_04_rook_lucan
if name:rook_coldwake and name:lucan_houndstooth and at:mr_ground and not flag.lethica_slain
interject name:rook_coldwake: Not a chair on the landing and locks on every door. You don't bolt a hospital from outside.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Look at the straps torn off that chair, if you please. Whatever sat there last had a remarkable reach.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Twelve morgue lockers and not a ledger in sight. My shield's knocker just clacked. I didn't touch it.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Someone kept a little shrine of keepsakes by the cots. As if they hoped to be forgiven.
endif
-> END

~ mr_grotto_05_cordelia_tobin
if name:cordelia_skein and name:tobin_hayward and at:mr_grotto and not flag.lethica_slain
interject name:cordelia_skein: The whole cavern's folded like a brain, Tobin. And the thing in the chains, the sheer volume of it.
interject name:tobin_hayward: That's no specimen, Cordelia. That's a fifty-year canker chained over a drain.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Look at the glow in those tanks. Lovely teal. Hold still, your primrose is wilting in the steam.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Leave my cuff be and step away from the glyphs. No clean seed ever grew in the dark.
endif
-> END

~ mr_ground_06_delphine_tobin
if name:delphine_ravelle and name:tobin_hayward and at:mr_ground and flag.lethica_slain
interject name:delphine_ravelle: The violet tubes have stopped humming, Tobin. Without Lethica it's just cheap velvet and cold tea.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Good riddance. The courtyard finally smells like plain rain. Even the fern's stopped shivering.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Masks on the floor, not a headliner left. Your Foolishness hasn't the heart for a pun.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Let the wind chimes be. You can't mend a house built on rot from the first row.
endif
-> END

~ mr_isle_07_lucan_tobin
if name:lucan_houndstooth and name:tobin_hayward and at:mr_isle and flag.lethica_slain
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: The violet glare's gone out of the brick, Tobin. Barnaby just sat down without a single yip.
interject name:tobin_hayward: The hexing's gone out of the mud. Those black irises will still take three winters to die back.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: The owl is preening as if he owns the estate. Eight out of ten for composure.
interject name:tobin_hayward: At least the rowboats are where we left them. Let's go before the damp gets into my burlap.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Agreed. Though I shall leave a stern note in my journal about the gardens.
endif
-> END
